node_modules/

# Editor and OS noise.
.vscode/
.idea/
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# NOTE on the knowledge build products. `scripts/build-knowledge.mjs` WRITES
# `resources/knowledge/stellaris/**` (TOML, derived from the hand-written `knowledge/*.md`) and
# `src/generated/knowledge.mjs` (the snapshot the server embeds). They are TRACKED, not ignored,
# for the reason the sibling `RStellarisGui` states in its own .gitignore: this project has no
# build step, `npm start` / `npx` runs `src/index.mjs` directly, and `package.json` ships `src`
# and `resources`. An ignored `src/generated/knowledge.mjs` would make a fresh clone a server with
# no knowledge base until someone ran the build - a clone that does not work is worse than a
# 745 KB file in the repository. `npm run build` regenerates both deterministically.
